1)How can we debug if any service is not getting launched , if it is deployed in openshift but still not able to open the aplication?
When an application is deployed but not accessible, debug at 4 layers:
POD → SERVICE → ROUTE/INGRESS → NETWORK/SECURITY
1)First ensure the application itself is running fine.
oc describe pod <pod-name>
oc logs <pod-name>
2️⃣ Validate Container Port & Service
oc exec -it <pod> -- netstat -tnlp
oc get svc
oc describe svc <service-name>
oc get routes
oc describe route <route-name
If everything is configured but still inaccessible, check network restrictions: 
oc get networkpolicy 
Sometimes app is running but keeps restarting or failing readiness checks:
I follow a layered approach to debug OpenShift access issues. First, I check if the pod is running and check logs.
Then I verify the service and ensure ports match. Next, I check the route configuration for external access. 
If all looks good, I review network policies, resource limits, and health probes.
Most issues usually occur due to incorrect service port mapping, failing readiness probes, or NetworkPolicy blocking traffic.

