23)if any production scenario can we resduce the pvc attached?
Yes, but only in certain storage systems and with caution — shrinking a PVC is risky and often not supported.
Because if the filesystem contains 60GB data and you shrink to 40GB → data corruption will happen.
Cloud block storage (EBS, Azure Disk) doesn’t support size reduction because:
Shrinking requires rewriting blocks and may corrupt data.
Recommended Production Approach
Create a new PVC with smaller size.
Copy data from old PVC to new PVC (using rsync or backup/restore).
Update the Deployment/StatefulSet to use the new PVC.
Delete the old PVC after validation.

24)Can we add pvc in the porduction environment ,once its is full?
Yes — you can add/extend PVC in production when it becomes full.
This is a common real-world scenario, and Kubernetes supports PVC expansion if the storage backend allows it.
StorageClass must support volume expansion (allowVolumeExpansion: true)
✔ PVC must use a supported CSI driver
✔ Filesystem expansion required inside the pod (K8s handles this automatically for most cases)
| Situation                     | Impact | Recommended Action             |
| ----------------------------- | ------ | ------------------------------ |
| DB pods crash due to no space | High   | Expand PVC ASAP + clean logs   |
| Static content                | Medium | Expand or use external storage |
| Logs filled the volume        | Medium | Rotate logs or move to sidecar |




